From 3568c2dd5a24690a4076abf1fb4102ddd70c284b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:27:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][dvbridge] The IPT tunnel reads PQ from tables made in
 double precision

Pass 9 computed the PQ EOTF and OETF of every pixel with exp, log, power
and division, written for float (series, P and T from logarithms of
ratios): 18 exponentials and logarithms and about 9 divisions a pixel,
whose precision is in the end that of each GPU's own functions.

Read PQ from two tables made once in double precision instead:
- the EOTF: a quadratic in each cell of 1/4096 of [2^-6, 1] and of 1/256
  of each octave of [2^-22, 2^-6), the cell found from the bits of the
  float, 0 below 2^-22 (128 KiB);
- the OETF: a quadratic in each cell of 1/128 of each octave of
  [2^-126, 2), the value at the start of a cell held as two floats
  (256 KiB).
L'M'S' are kept as the high part and the rest, so that P and T come
from L' - M' and S' - M' without a difference of two rounded values.
A pixel is then six fetches and plain arithmetic, the same on every GPU.
Dividing by the code scale becomes a multiplication by its exact
reciprocal (the same values).

Against ST 2084 in double precision over a dense sample, with the
entries in float, the tables are within 2.6e-5 of a code (the EOTF
taken back to PQ) and 3.5e-6 of a code (the OETF).

Measured with the software bridge on the 14 pictures of a profile 7
FEL stream, against the chain in double precision: 0.008 % of the I,
0.007 % of the P and 0.005 % of the T one code off, never more, where
the functions gave 0.043 %, 0.029 % and 0.036 %. The compute pass and
the fragment passes give the same bytes.
---
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_source.c | 308 ++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_source.h |   9 +-
 2 files changed, 206 insertions(+), 111 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_source.c b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_source.c
index 325abbd..6e52263 100644
--- a/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_source.c
+++ b/tools/dvbridge/dvbridge_source.c
@@ -1676,32 +1676,31 @@ struct common_uniforms {
 };
 /* 9. Hades: the IPT tunnel (dvbridge_source_to_ipt()): the codes of a pixel of the composer's YCbCr
  * picture in IPT-PQ-c2, in floats; the luma of the picture (9a, a float a pixel) and its rows of
- * 4:2:2 (9b, as pass 2 lays them out). The chroma between the pairs is Lanczos 6 in integers, the
- * filter of pass 2. Outside the active picture nothing is read: the transport is black there.
+ * 4:2:2 (9b, as pass 2 lays them out), or both in one compute pass (9c). The chroma between the
+ * pairs is Lanczos 6 in integers, the filter of pass 2. Outside the active picture nothing is read:
+ * the transport is black there.
  *
- * The chain is written so that float keeps the precision of its inputs, not as SMPTE ST 2084 writes
- * it:
- *  - the EOTF with q = 1 - N^(1/m2) = -expm1(ln(N) / m2) by its series, as libplacebo-9942 writes
- *    it: c2 - c3 N^(1/m2) is a difference of numbers close to each other above a few cd/m2;
- *  - the OETF as exp(m2 log1p(-w)), w = k (1 - t) / (1 + c3 t), t = l^m1, k = 1 - c1 = c2 - c3:
- *    (c1 + c2 t) / (1 + c3 t) is 1 - w, a number close to 1 whose float loses most of w, which
- *    the power m2 = 78.84 then makes a relative error 79 times its size;
- *  - P and T from the differences L' - M' and S' - M' (the rows of the inverse of YCCtoRGB that
- *    give them sum to 0, as the first column of YCCtoRGB is 1), made from L - M and S - M without
- *    a difference of the values in PQ: L' - M' = M' expm1(m2 (log1p(-w_L) - log1p(-w_M))), the
- *    logarithm of the ratio of 1 - w_L to 1 - w_M from w_M - w_L = k (1 + c3) (t_L - t_M) /
- *    ((1 + c3 t_L) (1 + c3 t_M)), and t_L - t_M = t_M expm1(m1 log1p((L - M) / M)); each series
- *    where its argument is at most 1/4 (beyond, the difference of the two logarithms, or
- *    exp(x) - 1, loses nothing); and rounded about 0, 2048 added after: at 2048 a float has
- *    1/4096 of a code, near 0 far less.
- * Every series is exact to 1e-9 or better on its range. Measured against the chain in double
- * precision on 14 pictures of a profile 7 FEL stream, on Mesa's software OpenGL ES: written as
- * ST 2084 writes it, 0.58 % of the I, 3.6 % of the P and 0.97 % of the T were one code off (up
- * to 6.7 % of the P of a picture where the composer's own chroma is); written so, 0.036 %, 0.034 %
- * and 0.041 % (at most 0.11 % of those samples of a picture), never more than one code. That is
- * of the order of single precision itself (the same chain on the processor, each operation
- * rounded once, is off on 0.003 % to 0.045 % of the samples of five of them): exact codes would
- * take more than the single precision that OpenGL ES 3.0 has. */
+ * PQ is read from two tables made once in double precision (ipt_tables()): no exp, log, power or
+ * division in the shader, whose precision would then be that of each GPU's own functions.
+ *  - The EOTF of each of R', G' and B': a quadratic in each cell of 1/4096 of [2^-6, 1] and of 1/256
+ *    of each octave of [2^-22, 2^-6) (the cell from the bits of the float), 0 below 2^-22 (ST 2084
+ *    gives 0 up to 2^-20.4). Against the EOTF in double precision over a dense sample, with the
+ *    entries in float: within 6.2e-8 of Y (relative, where Y > 1e-6), 2.6e-5 of a code taken back
+ *    to PQ.
+ *  - The OETF of each of L, M and S: a quadratic in each cell of 1/128 of each octave of [2^-126, 2)
+ *    (again from the bits of the float), its value at the start of the cell held as two floats (hi +
+ *    lo); within 3.5e-6 of a code. L'M'S' are kept as hi and the rest, not added.
+ *  - I from the hi and the rests; P and T from L' - M' and S' - M' (the rows of the inverse of
+ *    YCCtoRGB that give them sum to 0), each the difference of the hi (exact where they are close)
+ *    plus that of the rests: no difference of two values rounded in PQ, which the matrix of P and T
+ *    would multiply.
+ * Measured against the chain in double precision on 14 pictures of a profile 7 FEL stream, on
+ * Mesa's software OpenGL ES: 0.008 % of the I, 0.007 % of the P and 0.005 % of the T one code off,
+ * never more. Before, as ST 2084 writes it in floats: 0.58 %, 3.6 % and 0.97 %; with exp and log
+ * written for float (libplacebo-9942's series, P and T from logarithms of ratios): 0.043 %, 0.029 %
+ * and 0.036 %. What is left is the single precision of the matrices: the chain with PQ exact and
+ * each matrix product rounded once to float, emulated on the processor, is off on 0.008 %, 0.007 %
+ * and 0.001 % of them. */
 #define IPT_HEAD "#version 300 es\n" IPT_BODY
 /* (Hades: and 9c, the compute form, after its own first line) */
 #define IPT_BODY                                                                                  \
@@ -1715,50 +1714,33 @@ struct common_uniforms {
     "uniform ivec4 active_box;\n" /* x0, y0, x1, y1 of the active picture, in the picture */          \
     "uniform ivec2 pairs;\n"  /* the first and the last pair of the active picture */             \
     "uniform int hweights[12];\n"                                                                 \
-    "const float m1 = 2610.0 / 16384.0, m2 = 2523.0 / 4096.0 * 128.0;\n"                          \
-    "const float c3 = 2392.0 / 4096.0 * 32.0;\n"                                                  \
-    "const float k = 672.0 / 4096.0;\n" /* 1 - c1 = c2 - c3, exactly */                           \
-    "vec3 expm1_series(vec3 x)\n" /* |x| <= 1/4 */                                                \
-    "{\n"                                                                                         \
-    "    return x * (1.0 + x * (1.0 / 2.0) * (1.0 + x * (1.0 / 3.0) * (1.0 + x * (1.0 / 4.0)\n"    \
-    "           * (1.0 + x * (1.0 / 5.0) * (1.0 + x * (1.0 / 6.0) * (1.0 + x * (1.0 / 7.0)\n"      \
-    "           * (1.0 + x * (1.0 / 8.0))))))));\n"                                               \
-    "}\n"                                                                                         \
-    "vec2 expm1_series(vec2 x)\n"                                                                 \
-    "{\n"                                                                                         \
-    "    return expm1_series(vec3(x, 0.0)).xy;\n"                                                 \
-    "}\n"                                                                                         \
-    "vec2 expm1_any(vec2 x)\n"                                                                    \
-    "{\n"                                                                                         \
-    "    return mix(exp(x) - 1.0, expm1_series(clamp(x, -0.25, 0.25)),\n"                         \
-    "               lessThanEqual(abs(x), vec2(0.25)));\n"                                        \
-    "}\n"                                                                                         \
-    "vec3 log1p_series(vec3 u)\n" /* |u| <= 1/4: 2 atanh(u / (2 + u)) */                          \
+    "uniform highp sampler2D eotf_table, oetf_table;\n" /* dvbridge_source_to_ipt() */            \
+    /* the PQ EOTF of e in [0, 1] from eotf_table: a quadratic in each cell, of 1/4096 from 2^-6 on, */ \
+    /* of 1/256 of an octave from 2^-22 to 2^-6 (cells 4096 on; e by the bits of its float), 0 below */ \
+    "float eotf1(float e)\n"                                                                      \
     "{\n"                                                                                         \
-    "    vec3 s = u / (2.0 + u), s2 = s * s;\n"                                                   \
-    "    return 2.0 * s * (1.0 + s2 * (1.0 / 3.0 + s2 * (1.0 / 5.0 + s2 * (1.0 / 7.0\n"            \
-    "           + s2 * (1.0 / 9.0 + s2 * (1.0 / 11.0))))));\n"                                    \
+    "    float f = e * 4096.0;\n"                                                                 \
+    "    int ju = min(int(f), 4095);\n"                                                           \
+    "    uint b = floatBitsToUint(e);\n"                                                          \
+    "    bool uni = e >= 1.0 / 64.0, zero = e < 1.0 / 4194304.0;\n"                               \
+    "    int j = uni ? ju : zero ? 0 : int(b >> 15u) - 22784;\n" /* 4096 - (105 << 8) */          \
+    "    float t = uni ? f - float(ju) : zero ? 0.0 : float(b & 32767u) * (1.0 / 32768.0);\n"     \
+    "    vec4 q = texelFetch(eotf_table, ivec2(j & 255, j >> 8), 0);\n"                           \
+    "    return q.x + t * (q.y + t * q.z);\n"                                                     \
     "}\n"                                                                                         \
-    "vec2 log1p_series(vec2 u)\n"                                                                 \
+    /* the PQ OETF of x from oetf_table: cells of 1/128 of an octave from 2^-126 to 2 (x by the bits */ \
+    /* of its float), each its value at its start as hi + lo and a quadratic for the rest; below 2^-126 */ \
+    /* (0, negative) PQ(0), cell 16383. As (hi, rest), not added: L' - M' and S' - M' are taken from */ \
+    /* the hi (exact where they are close) and the rests */                                       \
+    "vec2 oetf1(float x)\n"                                                                       \
     "{\n"                                                                                         \
-    "    return log1p_series(vec3(u, 0.0)).xy;\n"                                                 \
-    "}\n"                                                                                         \
-    "vec3 eotf(vec3 e)\n"                                                                         \
-    "{\n"                                                                                         \
-    "    vec3 x = log(max(clamp(e, 0.0, 1.0), vec3(1e-30))) * (1.0 / m2);\n"                      \
-    "    vec3 q = mix(-expm1_series(clamp(x, -0.25, 0.0)), vec3(1.0), lessThan(x, vec3(-0.25)));\n" \
-    "    return pow(max(vec3(k) - q, 0.0) / (vec3(k) + c3 * q), vec3(1.0 / m1));\n"               \
-    "}\n"                                                                                         \
-    /* the OETF of l as exp(m2 lam): its logarithm, t = l^m1, w and lam = log1p(-w) */            \
-    "void oetf_parts(vec3 l, out vec3 lnl, out vec3 t, out vec3 w, out vec3 lam)\n"               \
-    "{\n"                                                                                         \
-    "    lnl = log(max(l, vec3(1e-37)));\n"                                                       \
-    "    vec3 a = m1 * lnl;\n"                                                                    \
-    "    t = exp(a);\n"                                                                           \
-    "    vec3 rest = mix(1.0 - t, -expm1_series(clamp(a, -0.25, 0.25)),\n"                        \
-    "                    lessThanEqual(abs(a), vec3(0.25)));\n"                                   \
-    "    w = k * rest / (1.0 + c3 * t);\n"                                                        \
-    "    lam = log1p_series(clamp(-w, -0.25, 0.25));\n"                                           \
+    "    float v = min(x, 1.99999988);\n"                                                         \
+    "    uint b = floatBitsToUint(v);\n"                                                          \
+    "    bool tiny = !(v > 0.0) || b < 8388608u;\n"                                               \
+    "    int k = tiny ? 16383 : int(b >> 16u) - 128;\n"                                           \
+    "    float t = tiny ? 0.0 : float(b & 65535u) * (1.0 / 65536.0);\n"                           \
+    "    vec4 q = texelFetch(oetf_table, ivec2(k & 255, k >> 8), 0);\n"                           \
+    "    return vec2(q.x, q.y + t * (q.z + t * q.w));\n"                                          \
     "}\n"                                                                                         \
     "uvec2 pair(int n, int r)\n"                                                                  \
     "{\n"                                                                                         \
@@ -1771,51 +1753,49 @@ struct common_uniforms {
     "}\n"                                                                                         \
     "vec3 linear_of(float y, vec2 c)\n"                                                           \
     "{\n"                                                                                         \
-    "    return eotf(clamp(ycc_src * (vec3(y, c) / code_scale - off_src), 0.0, 1.0));\n"          \
+    "    vec3 e = clamp(ycc_src * (vec3(y, c) * (1.0 / code_scale) - off_src), 0.0, 1.0);\n"      \
+    "    return vec3(eotf1(e.x), eotf1(e.y), eotf1(e.z));\n"                                      \
     "}\n"                                                                                         \
